About Us

Planck Technologies is a company specialized in Software Development, dedicated to shaping futures and creating value through innovative IT solutions. By expanding teams and offering a comprehensive range of services—from Software Development and Infrastructure Management to Cybersecurity—we empower clients with all the expertise they need in one place. Inspired by the principles of quantum physics, we push beyond traditional boundaries to deliver customized solutions that redefine the IT landscape and drive shared success.




What will you do? (Location: Onsite, Brussels)

 * Analyze and optimize web proxy configurations across on-premises and cloud environments;
 * Validate and document exceptions within the security architecture;
 * Recommend improvements to strengthen security and operational efficiency;
 * Produce clear documentation and actionable reports;
 * Collaborate with cross-functional teams to enhance security measures.




What are we looking for?

 * Proven experience as a Cyber Security Expert or Security Specialist;
 * Strong technical knowledge of web proxies, infrastructure, and security architecture;
 * Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills with high attention to detail;
 * Strong communication skills to engage both technical and non-technical stakeholders;
 * Fluency in English is required, French is a plus.




Location: Onsite, Brussels




We are waiting for you!

We are looking for a SOC Specialist, to integrate the team of our client – a reference Portuguese company in the banking sector.

What will be your main tasks and responsibilities?


 * Developing 2nd and 3rd line monitoring, incident response and analysis within Security Monitoring and Control teams and CSIRT scope;
 * Maintain and supervise the development and evolution of threats and vulnerabilities;
 * Identify and promote initiatives for the detection of malicious activity in information systems and networks;
 * Ensure the alignment between monitoring and vulnerabilities management activities, in order to guarantee that information systems and networks are fully protected against threats;
 * Ensure the defenses against potential threats namely through the constant review of security events management, review and optimization of use cases, incorporation of new IOC’s in security systems according to security alerts and feeds;
 * Ensure threat hunting activities and develop security incidents reports;
 * Analyze, classify and follow on information security incidents and vulnerabilities;
 * Define and design containment and eradication measures according to incident types;
 * Refine and/or create rules and signatures for monitoring according fraud patterns related to digital channels.



What is required from you?


 * Academic background in Computer Engineering, Information Systems or other similar area;
 * Previous professional experience in the areas of incident responde and analysis, security operation centres (SOC), practical roles of cybersecurity with a strong knowledge in security architectures and technologies;
 * Knowledge in the use of SIEM and SOAR tools;
 * Knowledge in Lean/Agile/DevOps principles;
 * Good analytical skills, critical sense, logic and structured thinking and ability to solve complex problems;
 * Ability to adapt and propose solutions in order to overcome challenges and obstacles;
 * Good relational and communicational skills;
 * Fluency in English (written and spoken).



Sounds like you? Send us your CV and let’s talk!

About the Company - Sysmatch is an IT Consultancy and Outsourcing Company with a wide range of technological skills, resulting from the accumulation of know-how and the experience of our consultants, allowing the implementation of solutions adapted to the needs of our clients, privileging their robustness and scalability. More than two decades in the IT market, we present ourselves as a flexible, adaptable, innovative and forward-looking Company.







About the Role: SOC- Security Engineer (Hybrid)










Required Skills

 * Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Engineering, Networks, Cybersecurity, or related fields;
 * Proven experience in SOC environments or similar operational security roles;
 * Solid knowledge of SIEM (e.g. Microsoft Sentinel, QRadar); EDR/XDR (e.g., Defender for Endpoint, CrowdStrike).
 * Familiar with Firewalls (DLP, CASB, NAC, IDS/IPS);
 * Network protocols and system administration (Windows/Linux);
 * Scripting (PowerShell, Python, Bash) for task automation;
 * Familiarity with Identity and Access Management (IAM) practices.







Relevant Certifications (preferred):

 * Microsoft SC-200 / SC-300
 * CompTIA Security+, CySA+
 * CEH, OSCP, GIAC
 * ZTNA / Zero Trust certifications (e.g., Palo Alto ZTNA, Forrester Zero Trust)







What we offer:

 * A dynamic project in a well-regarded client at an international level;
 * Salary classification according to the experience shown;
 * Career development with intervention in ambitious and innovative technological projects;
 * Good working environment with young and dynamic teams;
 * Personalized follow-up to each consultant;
 * Integration into Sysmatch staff with access to all company activities;
 * You will be part of our trainings and Team Building events;
 * A network of hundreds of partnerships with companies in countless sectors that offer you exclusive discounts (health, wellness, travel, gastronomy, culture, leisure, training, etc).




Recruitment, selection and integration process:

The first contacts will be made by phone call or video call.

We are prepared to ensure the monitoring and integration of new employees and support them in this new phase of their professional career.

We're fast learners, hard workers, natural collaborators... and we Make Modern Happen!




Our ambition is to unlock the potential of our digital world so that organisations everywhere can innovate and thrive securely. We aim to achieve this goal by bringing together the world’s most talented people and the most powerful technologies, combining them to address our customers' challenges and to build something stronger together.




If you share our vision, join us!




Right now, we are looking for a SOC Cybersecurity Analyst to integrate our internal team.




Your responsibilities include:




 * Monitoring security alerts generated by tools such as SIEM (Microsoft Sentinel), EDR, and others;
 * Performing the initial triage of alerts to identify potential threats and filter out false positives;
 * Following defined playbooks and procedures for incident response;
 * Investigating low to medium complexity security incidents by collecting evidence and analyzing logs;
 * Escalating more complex security incidents to senior analysts (L3) or other specialized teams;
 * Documenting all actions taken during the analysis and response to an incident in the appropriate ticketing systems;
 * Assisting in running vulnerability scans and tracking the status of identified vulnerabilities;
 * Contributing to the SOC's knowledge base by documenting new findings and suggesting improvements to procedures.







Your must have:




 * A degree in a technology-related field or equivalent practical experience;
 * At least 2 year of experience in a cybersecurity role;
 * Fluency in English (written and spoken) is essential;
 * Experience with alert/incident management in SIEM (preferably Microsoft Sentinel and Microsoft Defender) and EDR.
 * A basic understanding of networking concepts, operating systems, and cloud security;
 * Strong attention to detail and a methodical approach to problem-solving;
 * Good communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively in a team;
 * A curious and analytical mindset, with a passion for learning about cybersecurity.







We Value:




 * International experience;
 * Familiarity with Microsoft Security Tools and Services: Microsoft Sentinel, Microsoft Defender, etc;
 * Entry-level or associate certifications, such as CompTIA Security+ or Microsoft SC-200 (Security Operations Analyst Associate).







We offer:




 * Regular professional development;
 * Health insurance, with family package;
 * Office facilities for meals and snacks;
 * Regular teambuilding programs;
 * Friendly workplace.







Workplace: Lisbon/Porto - Hybrid




Claranet, Make modern happen!

With just over 7 years of experience in the Portuguese market, we share our DNA with more than 200 workers and position our offer according to 3 lines of service:

 * Strategy (Outsourcing, NeXel, Team as a Service, Tech Academies);
 * R&D (Bootcamps, POC, Tech Lab);
 * Nearshore.




In ADENTIS, we focus on PEOPLE. This is our emotional salary:

 * Great Work-Life balance;
 * Very flexible organizational routine;
 * Health benefits (for you and your family);
 * Team Building activities;
 * Over 300 protocols to offer you great discounts in different areas;
 * Continuous professional development sponsored by our Training and Certification Department;
 * Regular feedback on your performance through a personalized plan;
 * Comprehensive career plan and progression involving assertive performance reviews.




Responsibilities:

 * Design, implement, and optimize advanced security operations frameworks, ensuring scalability, reliability, and compliance with industry best practices;
 * Operate and evolve Google Security Operations tools (Chronicle, Siemplify, etc.), integrating them with existing environments and ensuring proactive detection and response capabilities;
 * Lead incident response activities, from triage to resolution, providing technical expertise and post-incident analysis to strengthen security posture;
 * Define and enforce security standards, monitoring rules, and playbooks to guarantee consistent and effective protection across systems and services;
 * Mentor and support junior security analysts, fostering knowledge-sharing and skills development;
 * Collaborate with cross-functional teams (infrastructure, development, DevOps, business units) to align security strategies with organizational goals;
 * Stay up to date with emerging threats, vulnerabilities, and technologies, recommending improvements and innovative solutions to enhance SOC efficiency;
 * Produce clear documentation of processes, incident reports, and security architectures.




You must have:

 * Academic background in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Engineering, or related field (or equivalent experience);
 * 5+ years of experience in cybersecurity, with at least 5 years in security operations or incident response;
 * 2+ years of hands-on expertise with Google Security Operations tools (Chronicle, Siemplify) or equivalent SIEM platforms (Splunk, QRadar, etc.);
 * Strong knowledge of threat detection, incident response, log management, and forensic analysis;
 * Experience with automation, scripting, and orchestration (e.g., Python, Bash, SOAR platforms);
 * Familiarity with cloud environments (Google Cloud Platform preferred, AWS/Azure as a plus);
 * Deep understanding of security frameworks, compliance standards, and best practices (e.g., MITRE ATT&CK, NIST, ISO 27001);
 * Excellent teamwork and communication skills in English (speaking and writing);
 * Relevant certifications are a plus (e.g., Google Professional Security Engineer, GCIA, GCIH, CISSP, CISM).




If you want to be part of a real People First organization, join us! Send your CV to andre.lago@adentis.pt

